    "body": "I think if we link above to `[=legacy selector alias=]`, we can probably lose this entire paragraph. Also I think this is covered by https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#compat, in particular \"All other [pseudo-elements](https://www.w3.org/TR/selectors-4/#pseudo-element) whose names begin with the string “-webkit-” (matched [ASCII case-insensitively](https://infra.spec.whatwg.org/#ascii-case-insensitive)) and that are not functional notations must be treated as valid at parse time.\"\n\nOr we could simplify to something like \"A selector containing an alias from the table above must be treated as if the alias were replaced by the corresponding unprefixed pseudo-element, including for matching and specificity.\" if you want to be more verbose.",
